"<p>Nitrobase uses <strong>Traefik v3</strong> (<code>nitrobase-traefik</code>) with flat dynamic route files under <code>/etc/nitrobase/traefik/dynamic/app-&#x3C;key>.yml</code> so routing changes apply immediately with zero proxy restarts.</p>\n<h2>Free Automatic Domains (<code>sslip.io</code>)</h2>\n<p>When you deploy a routed app without specifying a custom domain, Nitrobase automatically provisions a free <code>*.sslip.io</code> domain (configurable via <code>FREE_DOMAIN_PROVIDER</code>) pointing to the server's public IP, complete with an automatic Let's Encrypt HTTPS certificate.</p>\n<h2>Adding Custom Domains</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>At your DNS provider, create an <strong>A record</strong> (or CNAME) pointing your domain (e.g. <code>app.example.com</code>) to your server's public IP address.</li>\n<li>Open your app in Nitrobase, go to the <strong>Domains</strong> tab, and add the domain.</li>\n<li>Nitrobase runs DNS checks, writes the updated Traefik dynamic route file, and Traefik automatically requests a TLS certificate from Let's Encrypt (<code>ACME_EMAIL</code>, defaulting to the instance administrator's email).</li>\n<li>After deploying or changing routes, Nitrobase automatically re-checks domain reachability and TLS status after <code>DOMAIN_RECHECK_DELAY_MS</code> (default <code>20s</code>).</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Multi-Service &#x26; Path Routing</h2>\n<p>Templates can declare multiple routed services and path prefixes in <code>[[domains]]</code>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Primary domain:</strong> Assigned to the primary service (e.g. <code>app.example.com</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>Secondary subdomains:</strong> Additional services receive <code>&#x3C;subdomain>.&#x3C;domain></code> (for example, RustFS routes the S3 API on <code>app.example.com</code> and the console on <code>console.app.example.com</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>Path-based routing:</strong> Services on the same host can be mounted under specific path prefixes (longest prefix wins)—for example, Appwrite routes console on <code>/</code>, API on <code>/v1</code>, and realtime on <code>/v1/realtime</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Basic auth:</strong> Templates can declare <code>basic_auth</code> middleware backed by bcrypt-hashed credentials (<code>0600</code> file).</li>\n<li><strong>Extra domain policies:</strong> Some apps (such as auth-sensitive backends) warn or refuse extra domains on a service when sign-in only works on the primary domain.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Certificate Expiry Monitoring</h2>\n<p>Nitrobase scans every managed domain's TLS certificate daily (<code>CERT_SCAN_CRON</code>, default <code>23 6 * * *</code>) and emits <code>cert.expiring</code> (within <code>CERT_EXPIRY_WARNING_DAYS</code>, default <code>14</code> days) or <code>cert.error</code> notification events if a renewal fails.</p>\n<h2>Panel Domain (HTTPS for Nitrobase)</h2>\n<p>Configure a custom HTTPS domain for the Nitrobase panel itself either at install time (<code>--domain panel.example.com</code>) or later in <strong>Settings → Instance → Panel domain</strong>. Once enabled, set <code>PANEL_BIND=127.0.0.1:3000</code> in <code>.env</code> so plain HTTP is no longer exposed on the host.</p>"